Subject: Omit nil :sentinels from Sidekiq redis options
Origin: DHI-internal (Sidekiq 7 / redis-client compatibility)
Description: Upstream redis_options always sets sentinels:
 redis_sentinel_options. When redis_sentinels is unset that value is nil.
 Sidekiq 7 (redis-client) treats a present :sentinels key as sentinel mode
 and calls nil.map, so a plain redis_url probe returns HTTP 500 on /sidekiq.
 Only set :sentinels when redis_sentinel_options returns an Array.
Forwarded: not-needed (DHI Sidekiq 7 bump; upstream still pins Sidekiq 6.5.12)
Upstream source: https://gitlab.com/gitlab-org/ruby/gems/gitlab-exporter/-/blob/16.10.0/lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb
Base tree:
 Package: gitlab-exporter
 Tag: 16.10.0
 Layout: repository root after git checkout of tag 16.10.0
Files: lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb

diff --git a/lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb b/lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb
--- a/lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb
+++ b/lib/gitlab_exporter/sidekiq.rb
@@ -196,10 +196,11 @@ module GitLab
       def redis_options
         options = {
           url: @opts[:redis_url],
-          sentinels: redis_sentinel_options,
           connect_timeout: 1,
           reconnect_attempts: 0
         }
+        sentinels = redis_sentinel_options
+        options[:sentinels] = sentinels if sentinels.is_a?(Array)
 
         %i[username password].each do |credential|
           options[credential] = @opts[:"redis_#{credential}"] if @opts.key?(:"redis_#{credential}")
